ence: Candidate A not discussed much, D not discussed. But we still need to cover them before final. However we can still give recommendation now, but we must ensure we still cover A and D later. The instruction says we should still cover all candidates before final recommendation, but we can still give provisional recommendation now. It's okay to still discuss A and D later.\n\nWe need to decide whether to stick with B, switch to C, or maybe propose D or A. Let's evaluate.\n\nCandidate A: strengths: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities. Concerns: sometimes not good at taking criticism, eats unhealthily. No info on stress resilience, crew cooperation, reliability. Could be good but health concerns.\n\nCandidate D: strengths: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Concerns: regarded as arrogant, loner, weak leadership, hot temper. No info on stress resilience, crew cooperation.\n\nGiven the current evidence, C has strong stress handling, decision quality, crew positive atmosphere, but lacks reliability record and egocentric behavior. B has strong reliability (very conscientious) and stress handling, but uncooperative and nasty remarks. Which is more critical? Crew cooperation is essential. Egocentric may be less severe than overt uncooperative behavior. However lack of reliability record is a big gap. But we have no reliability record for any candidate except C is known to be 100% reliable? Wait note: In original notes: \"Candidate C is known to be 100% reliable.\" Yes! In the candidate information list: \"Candidate C is known to be 100% reliable.\" That is a fact! I missed that earlier. Indeed, the notes include: \"Candidate C is known to be 100% reliable.\" So we have reliability evidence for C. Good. So C has reliability, stress handling, decision quality, positive crew atmosphere. Concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. Those are less severe than B's uncooperative nasty remarks. So C seems strongest.\n\nThus Agent 2 should align with Candidate C. We need to reference that C is known to be 100% reliable (explicit fact). Also mention stress handling (keeps calm in crisis). Also mention positive crew atmosphere. And note B's uncooperative behavior. So we can reaffirm recommendation for C.\n\nWe also need to note that we still need to discuss A and D later, but for now we recommend C.\n\nThus produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: \"I agree with Agent 1, and given C's 100% reliability, calm under pressure, positive crew atmosphere, I maintain recommendation for C. B's uncooperative behavior remains a serious concern. A and D still need discussion, but based on current evidence C is best.\"\n\nMetadata: vote Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
